#039;ve been playing around with different ideas for my invitations. After many hours I finally came up with a design that met my vision. I decided to go with a pocket style invitation and use an embossing technique for the images.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I probably invested close to 75 hours into my invitations but most of that time was because I kept changing my mind :rolleyes:. Once I committed to a design I would say the whole process from designing the layouts in Photoshop to putting the last postage stamp on the outer envelope took me 7 hours to make 25 invitations.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For those of you interested in my fonts, I downloaded them for free from &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/1001freefonts.com&#039;&gt;http:\/\/1001freefonts.com&lt;\/a&gt;. I used:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Last names on invite &amp;amp; headings for inserts: Castellar&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;First names on invites and other \"scrolly\" text on the RSVP card:&amp;nbsp;Edwardian Script ITC&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Most test on invite&amp;nbsp;&amp;amp; inserts: Champagne &amp;amp; Limousines&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;After I worked out my wording for the invite and inserts I started by designing an image of sea coral in Photoshop then converted it to a vector using Illustrator. The original image was used for my invitations. I then cropped&amp;nbsp;a section of the original image and saved it in a separate vector file for the inserts, rsvp, and, \"one love\" square on the outside of the pocket. Once the images were ready I&amp;nbsp;contacted Dominion Stamps &amp;amp; Engraving (based out of Calgary, Alberta) &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.dominionstamps.com&#039;&gt;http:\/\/www.dominionstamps.com&lt;\/a&gt; and had them turn my custom images into 2 rubber stamps. I must say this company is fantastic to deal with and I highly recommend them. From the&amp;nbsp;time I first contacted them to the time I received my stamps was less than 5 days and I live on the other side of Canada!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I decided to cheat a little in the DIY process and ordered my paper and pockets from Cards and Pockets &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.cardsandpockets.com&#039;&gt;http:\/\/www.cardsandpockets.com&lt;\/a&gt; . Again they were fantastic to deal with.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Pocket invitations and outer envelope: Imperial Blue&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Inner envelope and invitation\/rsvp\/inserts: Snow white&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;RSVP envelope and invitation mat: Turquoise&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;With my invitations and enclosures all printed I was ready to start adding my custom images. I purchased my ink pads and embossing powder from Michael&#039;s. I used the Brilliance line of pigment ink in Rocket Red Gold color and Recollections embossing powder in clear. For the back of the RSVP envelope I used a heart stamp I found the clearance bin at Micheal&#039;s with ColorBox pigment ink in Robin&#039;s Egg and the same clear embossing powder used for my other images. It took a bit of practice to get the exact positioning of my images down but once I did my FI and I were off the races with our embossing assembly line (me stamping and dusting with embossing powder, him \"cooking\" the embossing powder with the heat gun). The embossing process is dead easy, even for amateur DIYers out there.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The attached pics are of the end result. I&#039;m happy with how they turned out but as a tip to other budget conscience Canadian brides, make a mock-up of your final product and take it to the post office. Because of my inserts and jute ribbon on the outside of the pocket (purchased from Michael&#039;s) my invitations were overweight and oversized so&amp;nbsp;I ended up having to spend about $60 on postage stamps :(&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[{"Id":33488,"Name":"all.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-57779100-1440339575.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-57779100-1440339575_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":33489,"Name":"inserts.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-00785700-1440339624.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-00785700-1440339624_thumb.jpg","Width":1000,"Height":800},{"Id":33490,"Name":"invite.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-43045300-1440339677.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-43045300-1440339677_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":33491,"Name":"pocketClosed.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-53047400-1440339722.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-53047400-1440339722_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":33492,"Name":"pocketOpen.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-67952600-1440339746.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-67952600-1440339746_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":33493,"Name":"rsvp.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-85988400-1440339778.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_08_2015\/post-284050-0-85988400-1440339778_thumb.jpg","Width":1000,"Height":750}],"Id":1903123,"PostDate":1440343606,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Even since I got engaged this past\u00a0January I've been playing around with different ideas for my invitations. After many hours I finally came up with a design that met my vision. I decided to go with a pocket style invitation and use an embossing technique for the images.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I probably invested close to 75 hours into my invitations but most of that time was because I kept changing my mind <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/rolleyes.gif' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':rolleyes:' \/>. Once I committed to a design I would say the whole process from designing the layouts in Photoshop to putting the last postage stamp on the outer envelope took me 7 hours to make 25 invitations.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>For those of you interested in my fonts, I downloaded them for free from <a href='http:\/\/1001freefonts.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/1001freefonts.com<\/a>. I used:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Last names on invite & headings for inserts: Castellar<\/p>\n<p>First names on invites and other \"scrolly\" text on the RSVP card:\u00a0Edwardian Script ITC<\/p>\n<p>Most test on invite\u00a0& inserts: Champagne & Limousines\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>After I worked out my wording for the invite and inserts I started by designing an image of sea coral in Photoshop then converted it to a vector using Illustrator. The original image was used for my invitations. I then cropped\u00a0a section of the original image and saved it in a separate vector file for the inserts, rsvp, and, \"one love\" square on the outside of the pocket. Once the images were ready I\u00a0contacted Dominion Stamps & Engraving (based out of Calgary, Alberta) <a href='http:\/\/www.dominionstamps.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.dominionstamps.com<\/a> and had them turn my custom images into 2 rubber stamps. I must say this company is fantastic to deal with and I highly recommend them. From the\u00a0time I first contacted them to the time I received my stamps was less than 5 days and I live on the other side of Canada!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I decided to cheat a little in the DIY process and ordered my paper and pockets from Cards and Pockets <a href='http:\/\/www.cardsandpockets.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.cardsandpockets.com<\/a> . Again they were fantastic to deal with.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Pocket invitations and outer envelope: Imperial Blue<\/p>\n<p>Inner envelope and invitation\/rsvp\/inserts: Snow white<\/p>\n<p>RSVP envelope and invitation mat: Turquoise<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>With my invitations and enclosures all printed I was ready to start adding my custom images. I purchased my ink pads and embossing powder from Michael's. I used the Brilliance line of pigment ink in Rocket Red Gold color and Recollections embossing powder in clear. For the back of the RSVP envelope I used a heart stamp I found the clearance bin at Micheal's with ColorBox pigment ink in Robin's Egg and the same clear embossing powder used for my other images. It took a bit of practice to get the exact positioning of my images down but once I did my FI and I were off the races with our embossing assembly line (me stamping and dusting with embossing powder, him \"cooking\" the embossing powder with the heat gun). The embossing process is dead easy, even for amateur DIYers out there.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The attached pics are of the end result. I'm happy with how they turned out but as a tip to other budget conscience Canadian brides, make a mock-up of your final product and take it to the post office. Because of my inserts and jute ribbon on the outside of the pocket (purchased from Michael's) my invitations were overweight and oversized so\u00a0I ended up having to spend about $60 on postage stamps <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"webgrl74@gmail.com","IpAddress":"99.224.73.70","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1437440585,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"2ndTimeMrs","Id":284050,"Name":"2ndTimeMrs","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.50.42.106","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79521,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a993ee6e4a78a951b62432605416614c","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Oh I love those! They&#039;re so pretty! I&#039;m a Jamaica bride too - October 2011 at Gran Bahia Principe Jamaica in Runaway Bay. We loved it and the Jamaican people. It&#039;s a beautiful place to get married! Congrats! I hope you keep us posted as things move along!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1903163,"PostDate":1440382763,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Oh I love those! They're so pretty! I'm a Jamaica bride too - October 2011 at Gran Bahia Principe Jamaica in Runaway Bay. We loved it and the Jamaican people. It's a beautiful place to get married! Congrats! I hope you keep us posted as things move along!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><em><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,255);\">I'm lucky enough to say yes again....October 20, 2015\u00a0<\/span><\/em>","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283462599,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1434318164","PhotoWidth":570,"PhotoHeight":541,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.150.95.42","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79521,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7669dc1e64f7011cb8dd9691d926726b","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;I&#039;m doing a pocketfold info guide for my oot and also used card and pockets templates... I am loving how&amp;nbsp;easy it is!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;These turned out great!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1903211,"PostDate":1440432817,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>I'm doing a pocketfold info guide for my oot and also used card and pockets templates... I am loving how\u00a0easy it is!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>These turned out great!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"malyna@gmail.com","IpAddress":"71.235.105.205","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1397443622,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277580.jpg?_r=1397779480","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"malyna","Id":277580,"Name":"malyna","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79521,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"64d9b0fd8e08b65d6f1274a640d8550c","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Great Job!!! &amp;nbsp;They look awesome!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1903234,"PostDate":1440439097,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Great Job!!! \u00a0They look awesome!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421446169,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1442083173","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"208.98.196.2","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79521,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c3b8d89a8283438cc9fb3b38d7fe7d98","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;so pretty!! Mine definitely didn&#039;t turn out that nice haha. Great job on these!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1903237,"PostDate":1440439393,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>so pretty!! Mine definitely didn't turn out that nice haha. Great job on these!\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359766704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1440029562","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"122.15.103.61","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79521,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5590c8e07e41f556c9c07ae69b54e7b8","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;So pretty!! Mine absolutely didn&#039;t turn out that first-rate haha. First-rate activity on those&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904906,"PostDate":1442474147,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>So pretty!! Mine absolutely didn't turn out that first-rate haha. First-rate activity on those<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rahulthakur01@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"122.15.103.61","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1438840568,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\